---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import ServiceLinks from '../../components/ServiceLinks.astro';
import site from '../../data/site.json';
import { dots } from '../../lib/patterns.js';
const ask = `mailto:${site.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Assistant adoption for our team')}`;
const bodyBg = dots();
---
<Base title="Assistant adoption: training your team" description="Four weeks beside your staff, on real work, so the Claude or ChatGPT account you already pay for gets used. They learn how to ask, how to check the page, and how to keep client files out of a personal chat.">
  <Hero variant="graph" seed={11} diagram="assistantsView" mapLabel="See how my AI system works" eyebrow="AI systems · Adoption" title="Teach your team to use the assistant">
    <p class="lede"><em>"We bought the AI and nothing changed."</em> Most teams get a login and a page of tips, then go back to the old way. I train your staff on their own work, so the account you already pay for gets used, and client files stay out of a personal chat. When I changed how one team worked with AI, their output rose 65%.</p>
    <a slot="actions" class="btn btn-secondary " href={ask}>Ask about adoption</a>
  </Hero>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="muted">Part of the <a href="/knowledge-assistants">AI system</a>: I set it up, then teach your team to use it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band-parallax">
    <div class="band-bg" set:html={bodyBg} aria-hidden="true" />
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What you get: four weeks of training</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><strong>Week 1.</strong> I sit in your workflow and write down where the time goes and which questions people ask each other every day.</li>
        <li><strong>Weeks 2–3.</strong> I work beside your staff on real tasks. They learn how to ask the assistant, how to check its sources, and when not to trust an answer. I write the house rules down so the habits outlast my visit.</li>
        <li><strong>Week 4.</strong> You get before-and-after numbers from your own records and a short list of what to do next.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2>Good fit if</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You have, or are getting, an AI system or assistant, from me or anyone else.</li>
        <li>You've already paid for AI tools and cannot say what changed.</li>
        <li>You want the numbers from your own records, not a vendor's slide.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><span class="tag">Fixed scope</span> <span class="tag">Four weeks</span> <span class="tag">Any industry</span> <span class="tag">Quote on scope</span></p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href={ask}>Ask about adoption</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ServiceLinks current="/knowledge-assistants" />
</Base>
